{{- /* internal/render/templates/finding.gohtml — one finding (§7.3):
a <details> element whose id attribute is the qualified id, verbatim,
no substitution, in either qualifier form (§8.1). Bead .1 seeds the
minimal <details>/id/body shape a structurally complete page needs;
bead .9 owns turning this into the real summary derivation (first
sentence of body, truncated at a word boundary to a 140-rune cap),
the priority-≥-7 open/closed default, the category/priority badges,
the data-* filter attributes (§5.1, §5.4), the anchors row, the code
excerpt ({{template "code"}}, bead .4's), and the suggestions
({{template "suggestion"}}, bead .9's own). Dot is htmlFindingView
(internal/render/html_view_finding.go). */ -}}
{{define "finding"}}
<details class="finding" id="{{.ID}}">
<summary>{{.ID}}</summary>
<p>{{.Body}}</p>
</details>
{{end}}
